    "description": "As a QA Software Engineer at CallRevu, I work at the intersection of software development, quality assurance, and customer experience to help deliver reliable, scalable products.\n\nMy responsibilities include designing and executing manual and automated test strategies, validating new features, identifying and reproducing software defects, and collaborating closely with developers and product teams throughout the software development lifecycle. I am currently leading the implementation of Playwright-based test automation, establishing scalable testing practices that will support future products and improve release quality.\n\nDrawing on my background in technical support and product expertise, I help bridge the gap between engineering and end users by translating real-world customer feedback into actionable product improvements. In addition to testing, I contribute to API validation, integration testing, technical documentation, process improvement, and cross-functional collaboration to ensure high-quality software releases.\n\nThroughout my career with the company, I have progressed from Technical Support to Support Lead, Tier II Support, QA, and now QA Software Engineer, giving me a unique perspective across customer success, product operations, and engineering.",
